# UTC Datetime: Always

RULE: All datetime objects must be timezone-aware UTC. Never use naive datetimes or deprecated utcnow().
WHY: Naive datetimes cause silent DST bugs, incorrect comparisons, and partition misalignment in GCS time-series data.
CODEX: 06-coding-standards/README.md

DO:
  from datetime import datetime, timezone
  now = datetime.now(timezone.utc)
  ts = datetime(2026, 1, 1, tzinfo=timezone.utc)

NEVER:
  datetime.now()         # naive — no timezone
  datetime.utcnow()      # deprecated since Python 3.12
  datetime.today()       # naive
  timezone-naive timestamps in any GCS schema or event metadata
